# The game's card in the menu, and what the game supports: one entity of keys, in the map
# list format. Every key is optional. A value with spaces MUST be in quotes.
#
# name         The title on the card. Unset, the name of the game's directory.
# description  The text on the card. It wraps to the card's width, and \n is a line break.
#              Keep it to a few lines.
# image        A PNG or JPG for the card, relative to the game's directory.
# gameplay     The gameplay modes, as g_gameplay names separated by spaces. Unset, all of them.
# maps         The tokens of a map's "games" key that Create Server lists, separated by spaces.
#              Unset, the name of the game's directory.
# practice     0 to offer no Practice. Unset, 1.

{
	name "Capture the Flag"
	description "Two teams. Steal the enemy flag, and bring it home to your own.\nWith the grapple hook and techs."
	gameplay "team_deathmatch team_instagib"
	maps "ctf"
}
